 "notes": "Video streaming cut from 115 services to 10 global leaders in m plus regional market leaders and best-known niche services in r (operator · market). Dropped as micro-regional or adult-adjacent: Aao NXT, Addatimes, Aha, Arre, Atrangii, Atresplayer Premium, BlazeTV, Bongo OTT, CSpace, Chaupal, D Anime Store, DMM TV, Dangal Play, EORTV, ETV Win, Epic On, Eros Now, FOD, Fox Nation, GagaOOLala, Hari Om, Hippiix, Hoichoi, Hungama Play, Kabla One, Kanccha Lanka, Klikk, Kutingg, Lemino, Lionsgate Play/+, Mahua Play, Mango TV, ManoramaMAX, MaskTV, Mastii, NammaFlix, Neon, Niri9, OneTheatre, Asia Premium Channel, PTC Play, Planet Marathi, Platform8, Prideplex, Raj Digital TV, Rakuten TV, Ratri, ReelDrama, Saina Play, ShemarooMe, Stage, Sun Direct GO, Sun NXT, Sundance Now, TVFPlay, Tarang Plus, Telasa, Tentkotta, Ultra Gaane/Jhakaas/Play, Veto, Vuclip, WATCH IT, WaahPlay, Watcho, AMC+, MGM+, Angel Studios, Discovery+. Genre focus and plan tiers moved to t. Sports: DIRECTV Stream brand ended April 2025 (now DIRECTV streaming); ESPN+ folded into ESPN Select/Unlimited (Aug 2025). Pay TV: DigitAlb (Albania) dropped as micro-regional. Kinds kept old s where carried over; Paramount+ owner per Wikipedia list (Skydance). Parallel connector out of credit; all sources via WebFetch."
